{"_id":"68a736178ec3d8323af164bc","nodeId":"jrH1qE6EnFXL4fTyYU8gR","roadmapSlug":"docker","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:03.460Z","description":"# Underlying Technologies\n\nDocker containers use Linux kernel technologies for isolation and resource management: namespaces for process isolation, cgroups for resource limits, and union filesystems for efficient layered storage. These enable lightweight, portable, and secure containers that share the host kernel.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Underlying Technologies","url":"https://www.docker.com/resources/what-container/#underlying-technologies","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dba6f"},{"type":"article","title":"Underlying Technologies - Medium","url":"https://medium.com/@furkan.turkal/how-does-docker-actually-work-the-hard-way-a-technical-deep-diving-c5b8ea2f0422","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dba70"},{"type":"video","title":"Containers - Namespaces, Cgroups and Overlay Filesystem","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wJdDWc6zO4U","_id":"69ca2cc033a0ad7a578dba71"}],"updatedAt":"2026-03-30T07:56:48.897Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04e0fb5fcb94d0416d80","title":"DataCamp - Introduction to Docker","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/zzDy1W"},{"_id":"6a5e04e0fb5fcb94d0416df4","title":"DataCamp - Containerization and Virtualization","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/GbEdZ2"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/docker/content/jrH1qE6EnFXL4fTyYU8gR.md"}